<title>USA: U.S. MMS sees FY 1998 OCS royalties at $4.38 bln.</title>
<headline>U.S. MMS sees FY 1998 OCS royalties at $4.38 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Minerals Management Service Thursday projected that its receipts from Outer Continental Shelf mineral leasing would rise 5 percent to $4.375 billion in fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>In MMS' fiscal 1998 budget plan, the agency also projected its onshore minerals leasing receipts would be $1.279 billion, up 6 percent from fiscal 1997's $1.208 billion.</p>
